item.description:
Our story AgeWell started over a conversation that many adult children know too well: &ldquo;Have you talked to mom today? Is she eating? Is she okay?&rdquo;
We&rsquo;re Adam, Brice, and Amitai — three software engineers in our late 40s and early 50s, each navigating the same challenge. Our parents are aging. They live independently. And we worry.
We tried the usual solutions: daily phone calls (that felt like check-ups), cameras (that felt invasive), medical alert pendants (that sat in drawers).
